# Fraud Detection API Service

A lightweight, containerized FastAPI application designed to serve a machine learning model (`RandomForestClassifier`) for predicting fraudulent transactions. 

## Project Structure

```text
/root/code/serving/
├── app.py        # FastAPI application (exposes /health and /predict)
├── Dockerfile    # Defines the python:3.11-slim container environment
└── model.pkl     # Trained RandomForest model artifact
Prerequisites
Docker installed on the host.

Pre-built Docker image: fraud-detector:v1

Deployment Instructions
Option 1: Deploy via Docker CLI
Run the container with the required bind-mount and port publishing:

Bash
docker run -d \
  --name fraud-api \
  -p 8085:8085 \
  -v /root/code/serving:/app \
  fraud-detector:v1
Verify that the container is running:

Bash
docker inspect fraud-api
Option 2: Deploy via Portainer UI
Access Portainer (running on port 9090).

Navigate to Containers -> Add container.

Configure the container parameters:

Name: fraud-api

Image: fraud-detector:v1

Network ports configuration: Map Host 8085 
→
→ Container 8085

Volumes tab: Map Host path /root/code/serving 
→
→ Container path /app

Click Deploy the container.

API Endpoints & Verification
1. Health Check
Endpoint: GET /health

Command:

Bash
curl http://localhost:8085/health
Expected Response:

JSON
{"status": "ok"}
2. Prediction Endpoint
Endpoint: POST /predict

Command:

Bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8085/predict \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"amount": 3200, "hour": 23, "num_tx_past_day": 5}'
Expected Response:

JSON
{"is_fraud": 1}

